PRE-REGISTERED 2026-08-30, BEFORE THE FIRST RUN ON THE ACTIVE BUILD.

The active build is canonical-10m-carve2, not precarve-craton-10m, so the cover statistics quoted above (35.9% on the floor, land median 365 m, 95th percentile 998 m, maximum 2,950 m, only 0.4% reaching 2 km) are a DIFFERENT build's and are re-measured here rather than carried.

THE DISPOSITION RULE, declared before the run. cover_thickness and the constant are BOTH readings of sourced material: Gleeson's 'on the order of 100 m' is the floor either way, and cover_thickness adds the export's own surviving cover on top of it. The spatially varying reading carries a real structure the constant drops, so under docs/src/practice/failure-modes.md class 16 it is preferred on physical grounds and NOT on whether it improves an agreement. The run measures what it costs. It is refused only on a STRUCTURAL failure: the solve not converging, the uniqueness identity not holding, or the water balance not closing at its declared bar.

WHAT IS MEASURED, both arms, on the same climatology and the same mesh:
  - the 95th percentile land depth, against GW-17's 52 m on Earth and against the constant arm on this build;
  - the median sink_fraction and the share of land above 0.9, which is the row's own prediction that cratonic cells move back towards the local recharge-and-evapotranspiration balance;
  - the share of land with at_surface set, which is the pathology config/pipeline.yaml's gate names;
  - the cover_thickness distribution itself on this build: share on the floor, median, 95th percentile, maximum, area-weighted mean, and the share reaching 2 km.

THE PREDICTION ON RECORD, from config/groundwater.yaml, written before any run: the depth range SHRINKS and cratonic cells move from lateral-flow control back towards the local balance. A loss of range with no gain in pattern is a real possible outcome and the run decides. Recording it here so the run can contradict it.

description:
vendor/exoplasim/exoplasim/__init__.py, in Model.modify(self, **kwargs):

    if key=="maxsnow":
        self.maxsnow=value
        if maxsnow:
            self._edit_namelist("landmod_namelist","DSMAX",str(self.maxsnow))
        else:
            self._rm_namelist_param("landmod_namelist","DSMAX")

`maxsnow` is not bound anywhere in modify() -- it takes only **kwargs -- and there is no module-level name of that spelling, so `model.modify(maxsnow=...)` raises NameError before it can edit anything. Every neighbouring branch in the same loop tests `value` or `self.<attr>`; this one alone tests a name copied from configure(), where it IS a parameter.

Found while wiring world-cwc. This project calls configure() and not modify(), so nothing here is affected today, and DSMAX also goes through configure_otherargs so a continuation cannot lose it. Filed because the same copy-paste shape is worth one grep over the rest of modify(): any branch testing a bare name rather than `value` or `self.` is the same defect.

The fix is `if self.maxsnow:`, and the same test's falsy-zero behaviour should be looked at while it is open -- maxsnow=0 would remove the key rather than set a zero cap.
